### Pilot ID card API — manual requests
###
### Set @token to a Descope session JWT (see README, "Getting a JWT for testing",
### or run tools/get-test-token.sh). Tokens live for minutes, not hours — if these
### start returning 401 having worked earlier, get a new one before debugging.

@host = http://localhost:5217
@token = PASTE_A_DESCOPE_SESSION_JWT_HERE

### 1. No token at all — expect 401 with a ProblemDetails body, not an empty one
GET {{host}}/api/idcard/me

### 2. The caller's own card — expect 200
GET {{host}}/api/idcard/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3. The caller's own card by route id — expect 200
GET {{host}}/api/idcard/member-alice
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. Another member's card — expect 403, and this is the one that matters
GET {{host}}/api/idcard/member-bob
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. A garbled token — expect 401
GET {{host}}/api/idcard/me
Authorization: Bearer not.a.jwt
